WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.729
A laptop can support portable experimentation and smaller models but has thermal and power limits.

00:00:07.729 --> 00:00:13.584
A workstation or gaming PC offers discrete GPU options and expansion.

00:00:13.584 --> 00:00:19.439
A mini PC favors compact low-power service for appropriately sized workloads.

00:00:19.439 --> 00:00:30.447
Apple Silicon uses unified memory shared by CPU and GPU, which can make larger model loading practical within total capacity and bandwidth.

00:00:30.447 --> 00:00:36.771
NVIDIA, AMD, and CPU-only systems use different acceleration paths and software support.

00:00:36.771 --> 00:00:44.031
GPU servers can provide memory, concurrency, remote management, and sustained cooling for multiple users.

00:00:44.031 --> 00:00:51.760
A private cloud instance can shift hardware ownership while retaining organizational network and access controls.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:56.679
Its data path and provider responsibilities still require review.

00:00:56.679 --> 00:01:04.408
Size CPU, GPU, VRAM or unified memory, system RAM, storage, network, power, and cooling together.

00:01:04.408 --> 00:01:12.136
Model weights, context cache, runtime overhead, users, documents, embeddings, and other applications compete for resources.

00:01:12.136 --> 00:01:18.929
Storage planning includes models, knowledge sources, indexes, chat data, logs, backups, and updates.

00:01:18.929 --> 00:01:24.315
Networking includes local access, remote administration, integrations, isolation, and bandwidth.

00:01:24.315 --> 00:01:30.171
An assistant can be local and still depend on remote services.

00:01:30.171 --> 00:01:36.494
Choose for the first workload with headroom, not the largest imaginable future.

00:01:36.494 --> 00:01:41.881
Measure a prototype on representative tasks before purchasing or scaling.

00:01:41.881 --> 00:01:48.673
The best platform is supportable, secure, recoverable, and fast enough for real users.

00:01:48.673 --> 00:01:50.781
Define availability needs.

00:01:50.781 --> 00:02:05.068
A personal assistant may tolerate manual restart, while a team service needs monitoring, controlled startup, capacity limits, maintenance windows, recovery documentation, and a fallback when the model is unavailable.
